# Phase 0 — Final state

## Outcome
**80 baseline → 3 architectural failures.** Phase 0 fs/env hardening complete.

## Network-dependent tests — fixed via local fixture

Switched 7 specs (73, 75, 76, 78, 79, 56, 59 + 1 test in 24, 82) off `https://example.com` onto a local Node `http.Server` fixture (`e2e/fixtures/test-server.ts`). Routes: `/` (instant), `/title-Example`, `/title-Other`, `/slow?ms=N` (delayed for loading-animation tests). Lazy start, single port-0 listener per worker, auto-close on `process.exit`.

Why: this machine's resolver returns `127.0.0.1` for `example.com` (VPN/Pi-hole/etc.), which broke any test that actually navigated to it. Local fixture is also faster + deterministic for timing-sensitive tests (`82-browser-loading-animation`'s "during loading" assertion now uses `/slow?ms=2000`).

Confirmed all 88 tests across 73/75/76/78/79/82/56/59/24 pass locally.

